{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1535202-sovereign-population","id":1535202,"title":"Sovereign Population","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-06T15:36:04-07:00","id":1535202,"title":"Sovereign Population","content":"So, according to Crucible of Legends, there is a highly variable overall population of 200-300 Exigents at any time in Creation, rapidly rising and falling as individual Exigents are created or die. No known number for individual Exigent types is given however as far as I am aware. With that in mind, for Sovereigns, what would you all suggest is a good approximation for their (remaining) numbers? It's at least 10 just based on the notable characters mentioned in Across the Eight Directions, but would you say that 20, 30, 50 Sovereigns is a reasonable number overall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T16:54:26-07:00","id":1535382,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty good question actually - to be honest, i've something of a very strong hunch that Sovereigns, due to the particular mix of forces and circumstances involved in their making, do not quite count as Exigents but more of their own quite peculiar thing, at least when it comes to the matter of numbers.<br /> <br /> The fact each and every one of them comes to be through ritually bathing or interacting with the &quot;lake&quot; formed from what might be Aurora's remains only seems to reinforce this &quot;not playing by the same rules anymore&quot; feeling, so i'd say whatever numbers you decide you prefer, they not exactly &quot;poach&quot; on the Exigent totals in Creation per se, since if there's something that might be able to empower several exaltations, possible remnants of a dead Incarna kind of makes a good case on its own.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way, how large do you imagine their kingdom and the ruling family being? Plus, not exactly every one among the nation's elites has to be a Sovereign to have influence and respect in their halls of power. In fact i'd imagine that with all the ups &amp; downs involved in becoming a Sovereign, there must be a number of &quot;special individuals&quot; like sorcerers, god-bloods, thaumaturgists &amp; other types with a supernatural trick or two resulting of non-fatal failures, partial successes, works in progress and a number of other situations.<br /> Kind of like young dynastic children attempting all kinds of weirdness to &quot;jumpstart&quot; their exaltation so to speak, though with slightly more heft, i'd guess.<br /> <br /> So the real question is: how many &quot;people of import&quot;, be they Sovereigns, other exalts - damn, now i'm totally thinking of a Liminal resulting of someone's crazed attempt to ressurect a failed candate for Sovereign - sorcerers, mutants, god-bloods or more do you need to make a version of this magical kingdom suitable to your tastes and STing needs? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-31-2026, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T16:16:27-07:00","id":1535468,"title":"","content":"I believe that Across the Eight Directions list Sovereign numbers as more than 20. So a number between 20 and 30 seems reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T17:00:43-07:00","id":1535471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Great Cthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1535202-sovereign-population?p=1535468#post1535468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that Across the Eight Directions list Sovereign numbers as more than 20. So a number between 20 and 30 seems reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to know indeed, gives everybody a little more definition to work with - though on a little aside, the Fount of Glories being possibly inexhaustible (being described as both &quot;a potent Means for sorcerous workings&quot; and &quot;a source of raw Essence on par with the mightiest demesnes&quot;) and most mysterious source of power for all Sovereigns, it can still hide space for plenty of surprises.<br /> <br /> Individuals that failed to become Sovereigns and yet were not consumed or shattered by the seven-colored flame.<br /> Scions of royalty that awaken to sorcery or return as beings akin to a variety of god-bloods, spirits or more are possible.<br /> Or maybe someone comes out as something that looks like a Sovereign and yet different, manifesting different Anima powers and charms tied to abilities no Sovereign ever manifested a talent in?<br /> <br /> <i><b>Anomalies </b></i>of sorts, one might say. What might those (even more) unusual individuals touched by the Fount of Glories' majesty do in many struggles beside (or against) their Sovereign brethren?<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, Uiluru does not exist in some sort of limbo or vacuum - Queen Ulu had diplomatic entreaties with the Scarlet Empress in the Blessed Isle, meaning elements of the Dynasty and probably Sidereals &amp; Lunars are at least aware of their existence, what might involve all kinds of designs or plans from alliance to conquest, research or more.<br /> <br /> Also, Sapphire Talisman Apocrypha <i>by its simple existence </i>informs us of the fact one or more among the most puisant Sovereigns has had dealings with beings versed in Celestial Circle spells.<br /> Who could be any of the aforementioned exalts, powerful spirits, fae, ghosts or something else altogether, depending on the kind of stories one wants to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-26-2024, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T17:37:56-07:00","id":1535472,"title":"","content":"An entire Shaping Ritual based on the Font of Glories makes a lot of sense! And at the very least the Font is a good excuse to buy the mutation Merits for people living in Uiluru. A caste of blessed and cursed that fills some religious or mystic or social function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-12T06:38:32-07:00","id":1535485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Great Cthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1535202-sovereign-population?p=1535472#post1535472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An entire Shaping Ritual based on the Font of Glories makes a lot of sense! And at the very least the Font is a good excuse to buy the mutation Merits for people living in Uiluru. A caste of blessed and cursed that fills some religious or mystic or social function.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooohhh, a whole sorcerous initiation and associated shaping rituals &amp; supernatural merits connected to the Fount of Glories, that could jumpstart all kinds of craziness.<br /> <br /> Maybe ghosts of past candidates acting as unseen guardians or whisper spirits/echo elementals, akin to Cantata-of-the-Depths in its earliest days in the road of godhood, watching over the caves leading to its resting place. Many, many things one could add to the magical landscape of the kingdom, visible or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now on a whole different vein, it just crossed my mind that the Sovereigns imagery of crystaline constructs containing supernal flame that will sometimes rage beyond their cracks pouring destruction unto the world around them, when not shattering their holders altogether - damn, that actually also resonates <i><b>a lot</b></i> with the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Defiler_Caste\" target=\"_blank\">Defilers</a> from back in 2e. Enough to make for an alternate/apocryphal origin, at least as told by some local secret demonic cult, perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-12-2024, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}